WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.657
This is a small online shop running on Azure.

00:00:02.787 --> 00:00:04.757
A gateway uses the API.

00:00:04.887 --> 00:00:07.372
The web service also calls the API.

00:00:07.502 --> 00:00:11.541
The API reaches PostgreSQL through a service called
database.

00:00:11.671 --> 00:00:13.983
Web also uses a cache and storage.

00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:16.715
No single source sees that whole picture.

00:00:16.845 --> 00:00:18.956
Kubernetes describes the services.

00:00:19.086 --> 00:00:20.776
Network flows show calls.

00:00:20.906 --> 00:00:25.431
Azure inventory names the resources, and Azure Monitor
supplies readings.

00:00:25.561 --> 00:00:29.041
Adapters translate each report into rows with named
fields.

00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:32.503
Sattle builds a master graph from those observations.

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:34.850
Two queries turn it into a health model.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.872
The first finds the workload and its dependencies.

00:00:38.002 --> 00:00:41.334
The second applies signal rules and works out who is
affected.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.802
The example already ships with working definitions.

00:00:44.932 --> 00:00:48.695
For your own workload, connect the sources you have
permission to read.

00:00:48.825 --> 00:00:50.692
Choose the namespace and cluster.

00:00:50.822 --> 00:00:54.394
Here the namespace is shop, and the cluster is aks-
synth.

00:00:54.792 --> 00:00:57.129
Your team decides what unhealthy means.

00:00:57.259 --> 00:01:03.286
For pg-shop, the supplied database rule trips after one
low minute and clears after two good minutes.

00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:07.686
It applies to servers of this type, so each server can
use the same rule.

00:01:08.083 --> 00:01:10.638
The workload query also encodes a judgment.

00:01:10.768 --> 00:01:13.376
Here a caller depends on the service it calls.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:18.112
If a call is optional in your system, change that rule
to represent your design.

00:01:18.242 --> 00:01:21.937
Sattle can then find matching instances as new evidence
arrives.

00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:23.798
Start with identity.

00:01:23.928 --> 00:01:28.083
The inventory record and the meter target share the
same Azure resource ID.

00:01:28.213 --> 00:01:30.139
Their evidence meets at one server.

00:01:30.269 --> 00:01:32.487
The Kubernetes service has a different key.

00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:34.437
A link says the server backs it.

00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:38.654
The paper calls the vocabulary of types and links an
ontology.

00:01:38.784 --> 00:01:41.311
A projection is a query that builds a new view.

00:01:41.441 --> 00:01:45.449
Watch several pod calls group into one link between web
and API.

00:01:45.579 --> 00:01:48.230
You can follow that link back to its evidence.

00:01:48.625 --> 00:01:50.181
The structure has versions.

00:01:50.311 --> 00:01:52.332
The readings form a time series.

00:01:52.462 --> 00:01:55.034
New readings can leave the structure unchanged.

00:01:55.164 --> 00:01:59.566
When a declared rule changes state, its result can
change the health graph.

00:01:59.696 --> 00:02:03.909
That separation keeps a busy meter from redrawing the
shop at every sample.

00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:07.941
At ten eleven, the database meter falls from one to
zero.

00:02:08.071 --> 00:02:11.380
The sample reaches the capture at ten twelve and one
second.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:13.786
The first low minute trips the authored rule.

00:02:14.208 --> 00:02:17.330
pg-shop now has an unhealthy signal of its own.

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.457
The database service relies on it.

00:02:19.587 --> 00:02:24.193
API relies on database, and both the gateway and web
rely on API.

00:02:24.323 --> 00:02:27.141
Health changes travel back toward those callers.

00:02:27.271 --> 00:02:30.011
The cache and storage stay healthy in this incident.

00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:32.507
The meter rises at ten fourteen.

00:02:32.637 --> 00:02:33.924
That is one good minute.

00:02:34.054 --> 00:02:37.023
At ten fifteen the second good minute clears the
signal.

00:02:37.153 --> 00:02:40.044
The same dependency paths now carry recovery.

00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:42.648
Rewind to the earlier cache incident.

00:02:42.778 --> 00:02:46.235
In the original run, web uses the overloaded cache.

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.039
Web and the shop are degraded.

00:02:48.169 --> 00:02:50.373
The API and gateway stay healthy.

00:02:50.792 --> 00:02:54.090
For a second run, we added one deployment update.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.410
The API now has a cache host setting naming the
existing Azure cache.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:05.449
The shipped structure query matches that host to
inventory and adds an API to cache dependency with
configuration evidence.

00:03:05.875 --> 00:03:08.847
Compare both runs at ten oh six and thirty seconds.

00:03:08.977 --> 00:03:13.205
With that extra link, the API and its gateway also
become degraded.

00:03:13.335 --> 00:03:16.227
The meter and health rules are identical in both runs.

00:03:16.357 --> 00:03:18.598
The different result comes from the new path.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.144
Here is a separate replay experiment.

00:03:21.274 --> 00:03:25.046
The API configuration names a new cache called offers-
cache.

00:03:25.176 --> 00:03:28.284
At first Azure inventory has no matching resource.

00:03:28.414 --> 00:03:31.177
The structure query cannot complete that link yet.

00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:34.887
Now add an Azure Resource Graph record for offers-
cache.

00:03:35.017 --> 00:03:39.774
Its type and name produce the host that the API
configuration already mentions.

00:03:39.904 --> 00:03:42.680
The same query adds the resource and the dependency.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:45.788
No new query was needed for this supported Redis type.

00:03:46.208 --> 00:03:48.473
The new cache shows up with unknown health.

00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:51.740
We supplied inventory, but no meter readings for it.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.034
A new resource type or a different naming convention
may need a new matching rule.

00:03:56.164 --> 00:04:01.641
A new signal needs an adapter or meter mapping and a
health rule when the existing ones do not cover it.

00:04:02.042 --> 00:04:06.474
In a live deployment the engine learns about changes
when its sources report them.

00:04:06.604 --> 00:04:10.966
It updates the affected results and sends a patch, a
list of graph edits.

00:04:11.096 --> 00:04:13.519
A collector falling silent leaves a gap.

00:04:13.649 --> 00:04:16.508
Silence alone never proves a resource was deleted.

00:04:16.917 --> 00:04:20.528
The Canvas starts from a snapshot and applies patches
in order.

00:04:20.658 --> 00:04:25.775
In the bundled static workload export, revision sixteen
shows the database outage.

00:04:25.905 --> 00:04:27.979
Revision eighteen shows recovery.

00:04:28.109 --> 00:04:29.570
Those are graph versions.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.163
The meter uses minutes.

00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:38.004
The white paper explains why updating just the changed
parts should agree with rebuilding from scratch under
its assumptions.

00:04:38.134 --> 00:04:41.605
Tests run an independent evaluator and compare results.

00:04:41.735 --> 00:04:45.857
The same recorded inputs and definitions let you repeat
the investigation.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:49.915
In the Canvas, open the workload tree and select pg-
shop.

00:04:50.045 --> 00:04:54.131
The origin marker identifies a component with its own
failing signal.

00:04:54.261 --> 00:04:59.762
The Inspector shows its earlier state, its new state,
and the graphs that support the result.

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:05.787
Follow the answer back through the workload health
query, the structure query, and the source records.

00:05:05.917 --> 00:05:11.954
To test a different interpretation, edit a draft in the
projection editor and preview its rows on a running
engine.

00:05:12.375 --> 00:05:14.210
The lab collects observations.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:16.742
The engine joins them with your definitions.

00:05:16.872 --> 00:05:18.916
The Canvas explains the result.

00:05:19.046 --> 00:05:23.872
In the walkthrough, switch on the new dependency, then
add the missing Azure inventory.

00:05:24.002 --> 00:05:26.454
Watch which parts of the same shop change.
